From: mscharged-port
Subject: New runtime: GX draws leave out bindings that did not change
Upstream-base: d664382f57002fbff143911c81b06b7e7a4b3ab4
Classification: host performance (feat/performance). Apply after 0131.

Every GX draw bound the uniform group, its texture group and its index range
again, although consecutive draws mostly share the first two and all use one
index buffer. With the new runtime a GX draw sets only the bindings that
differ from the previous GX draw of the pass; the index buffer stays bound
whole and each draw starts at its own first index (the same indices). A pass
start, a custom draw or any draw other than a GX draw (clears, pokes, RmlUi)
makes the next GX draw bind everything again.

